    "standalone_rule": "The rail carries geometry only — where a Unit stands and how far it reaches: FIXED, RESERVE, VIGIL, RANGE <n>, PRESENCE <n>. Every other standalone token is an ability, not a position, so it belongs in the text box: MEMORIALIZE, PREPARED, BOUND, INHERIT, LEVY. Rarity words drive the rail's rarity label and DEITY drives the type. A standalone token outside standalone_known still routes to the body, and the renderer flags it so a new keyword is noticed by design rather than absorbed silently.",
    "lead_rule": "The text before the em dash is a keyword lead when it is all-caps and at most three words; it renders in the bold weight. The whole rule always stays in the body.",
